load @term/seed/code/structure/algebra/clifford
  find clifford-algebra

# A geometric algebra: a Clifford algebra used as the language of geometry, where the single geometric product unifies
# the dot product (its symmetric part) and the wedge product (its antisymmetric part). Vectors, areas, and volumes live
# in one algebra, and rotations are conjugations by even versors. It is the same object as the Clifford algebra, named
# for its geometric use. The form carries the underlying Clifford algebra.
form geometric-algebra
  link algebra, like clifford-algebra
